{"content":"⚠️ **IMPORTANT: Transport/auth failures are misreported as "space not found"**

`_spaceIdFromKey` funnels every failure mode into `null`, and all callers translate `null` into `Confluence space not found by key: …`:

```dart
final results = _childrenResults(syncBodyOrError(resp));
if (results == null || results.isEmpty) return null;
```

On a curl transport failure `syncBodyOrError` returns the `{"error": "HTTP request failed: …"}` envelope (no `results` key → `null`); on a non-2xx response (e.g. **401 from a granular/scoped token that lacks the `read:space:confluence` scope**) the error body also decodes without `results`. Both are indistinguishable from a genuinely unknown key, so the user debugging a v2 token setup sees "space not found" when the real problem is auth or network.

The async counterpart (`ConfluenceClient.spaceIdFromKey`) surfaces the HTTP error because dio throws before the results parse.

Consider distinguishing the cases, e.g.:

```dart
final resp = SyncHttpClient.get(...);
if (resp.statusCode == 0 || !resp.isOk) {
  throw StateError('Confluence space lookup failed for key $spaceKey: ${resp.body}');
}
```

Callers already handle thrown `StateError`s from this area (`_SyncConfluencePageOps.createPage`, `_titleAndSpaceResponse`), and the tool bridge converts throws into tool errors, so this stays within the existing contract.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment1.md"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: v2 title-lookup failure path (unknown space) is untested**

Under v2, `_titleAndSpaceResponse` throws `StateError` when the space key cannot be resolved:

```dart
final spaceId = _spaceIdFromKey(config, space);
if (spaceId == null) throw StateError(_spaceNotFound(space));
```

This throw propagates out of `confluence_content_by_title`, `confluence_content_by_title_and_space`, `confluence_find_content*`, and `confluence_find_or_create` — a different error surface than `confluence_create_page`, which returns a `syncErr` envelope (and is tested). The v1 fixtures and the new v2 tests never exercise a title lookup with an unresolvable space, so this path — including the exact message the JS bridge turns into `Tool execution failed: Bad state: …` — has no coverage.

Worth one test, e.g. `confluence_content_by_title_and_space` with `space: 'NOPE'` under v2 asserting the throw/`Tool execution failed` outcome, so a future refactor cannot silently change this contract.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment2.md"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: hoist the duplicated version fetch out of the branch**

Both arms of the `if/else` fetch the version identically:

```dart
if (_isApiV2(_config)) {
  final version = _fetchVersion(contentId);
  ...
} else {
  final version = _fetchVersion(contentId);
  ...
}
```

Hoist `final version = _fetchVersion(contentId);` above the branch — one line less per arm and no risk of the two drift­ing apart:

```dart
final version = _fetchVersion(contentId);
final SyncHttpResponse resp;
if (_isApiV2(_config)) {
  resp = SyncHttpClient.put(... _updatePayloadV2(contentId, title, body, version + 1, historyComment));
} else {
  resp = SyncHttpClient.put(...);
}
```
